><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250515131816+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250515131818+10'00'" name="defa329b-a6e7-4350-ba20-1d1391543a29" page="5" coords="50.966354,192.218307,505.271759,192.218307,50.966354,177.457901,505.271759,177.457901,39.004822,181.787033,505.270721,181.787033,39.004822,167.026627,505.270721,167.026627,245.818573,179.300385,252.019302,179.300385,245.818573,168.827850,252.019302,168.827850,344.859802,179.300385,351.060547,179.300385,344.859802,168.827850,351.060547,168.827850,465.048126,179.300385,471.248840,179.300385,465.048126,168.827850,471.248840,168.827850,39.004852,171.299179,505.262085,171.299179,39.004852,156.538773,505.262085,156.538773,39.004852,160.867905,505.266785,160.867905,39.004852,146.107498,505.266785,146.107376,39.004700,150.379135,505.255554,150.379135,39.004700,135.618729,505.255554,135.618729,39.004730,139.947861,505.257996,139.947861,39.004730,125.187454,505.257996,125.187454,39.004700,129.460007,505.258118,129.460007,39.004700,114.699600,505.258118,114.699600,39.004730,119.028732,505.228363,119.028732,39.004730,104.268326,505.228363,104.268326,39.004730,108.540024,477.335571,108.540024,39.004730,93.779617,477.335571,93.779617,488.802094,108.540085,505.252441,108.540085,488.802094,93.779617,505.252441,93.779617,479.957703,106.053375,486.158447,106.053375,479.957703,95.580841,486.158447,95.580841,39.004700,98.108871,385.328003,98.108871,39.004700,83.348465,385.328003,83.348465,119.904404,95.622223,126.105133,95.622223,119.904404,85.149689,126.105133,85.149689,269.572510,95.622223,275.773254,95.622223,269.572510,85.149689,275.773254,85.149689" rect="38.543427,82.887192,505.733032,192.679581" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Despite the overwhelming evidence in favour of an external focus of attention, results in studies examining skilled performers have proved equivocal (</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#2095D0;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Bahmani et al., 2019</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>; </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#2095D0;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Fairbrother, Post, &amp; Whalen, 2016</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>; </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#2095D0;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Guss-west &amp; Wulf, 2016</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>; </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#2095D0;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Raisbeck, Yamada, &amp; Diekfuss, 2018</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>). This study examined the performance of skilled swimmers conducting a dive start under internal and external focus of attention conditions. Our results revealed no differences in variables that might indicate performance outcomes, suggesting that skilled performers may be robust to the detrimental effects of an internal focus. However, examination of the remaining kinetic and kinematic measures which provide insight into how the task is completed showed that swimmers had faster movement organization under an external focus, with greater average horizontal acceleration and earlier peak force timing data. An external focus may be beneficial for the organization of movement control in skilled swimmers, but may not have an immediate impact upon the outcome of the task. Therefore, findings provide further evidence for the stability of expert performance under changing constraints (</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#2095D0;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Couvillion &amp; Fairbrother, 2018</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>; </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#2095D0;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Pelleck &amp; Passmore, 2017</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>; </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#2095D0;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Porter, Anton, Wikoff, &amp; Ostrowski, 2013</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>; </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#2095D0;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Wulf, 2008</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>).</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="5" rect="544.252014,100.218307,728.252014,192.218307"
/></highlight
